            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Ying Janna Deng"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Tangy, peppery and a sweet. Tried it with a can of crushed tomato instead of ketchup as well, and it was still awesome, more smoky and less sweet tasting though.",
            "datePublished": "2012-03-21T01:57:38.610Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Ms Chef Esh"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I think the bacon drippings are the key to this recipe. I did not have Spanish parika, so I used smoked paprika instead...this sauce has a lot of depth, and I loved the fresh ginger and soy sauce in this. I made pulled pork BBQ in my slow-cooker with this sauce! Unbelievable BBQ sauce recipe!!!",
